& [DictatedQuestion]
  + execution of compiled lookahead may suggest the inference domain in which its functions should operate
  + sampling an optimal set of terms may reduce the time needed to execute a query in inference
  + identify a mechanism that selects the optimal terms needed to lay tracks so inference can work in a snap

& [SelectedMechanism]
  + StitchSelector is the candidate deterministic mechanism that compiles one bounded set of LookaheadStitch values for one exact subject scope model profile and horizon
  + TermCandidate is a source-bound semantic anchor distinction relation coordinate or cue considered for one stitch
  + StitchSetSelection is the retained candidate pool score account selected set rejected set uncovered account budget account and optimization receipt
  + the first mechanism is provider-free and deterministic; model-driven term generation or live calibration is a later separately governed experiment

& [CandidatePool]
  + governing requirements constraints denials and nonauthority boundaries supply mandatory candidates
  + the current subject objective dependency graph plan frontier file and symbol coordinates expected outputs and evidence gates supply action candidates
  + operational faults ambiguity records rejected routes and commonly collapsed distinctions supply contrastive candidates
  + prior attributed successful receipts may supply empirical candidates only when task model context compiler and authority identities correspond
  + ungoverned conversation unrelated repository state private reasoning secrets and hidden model state never supply candidates

& [StructuredTerm]
  + a bare keyword is insufficient because its meaning trajectory and stop condition may remain ambiguous
  + every selectable candidate binds subject semantic distinction or relationship intended transform scope source role and completion or invalidation cue
  + compact surface terms may be projected to the model while the full structured identity remains in the Cantor receipt

& [OptimizationObjective]
  + maximize governing-requirement coverage current-decision relevance ambiguity reduction action-coordinate relevance evidence-gate relevance and known-fault avoidance
  + minimize UTF-8 bytes token estimate redundancy overlap stale-distance unsupported inference and anchoring risk
  + satisfy every mandatory governing anchor before considering optional derived hints
  + select the smallest set that closes the declared coverage threshold under exact context and stitch ceilings
  + preserve uncovered obligations rather than pretending an optimal set exists when the budget cannot cover them

& [SelectionDirection]
  + normalize and deduplicate candidates by semantic identity rather than surface spelling alone
  + construct a coverage relation from each candidate to requirements decisions coordinates evidence and faults
  + prune dominated candidates whose covered set is a subset at equal or greater cost and risk
  + apply a deterministic bounded weighted set-cover or equivalent exact small-set search with stable tie breaking
  + emit one selected order based on governing precedence dependency order and projected placement role rather than arbitrary score order
  + retain why each candidate was selected rejected or left unresolved

& [InferenceDomainBoundary]
  + inference domain means an explicit semantic working domain induced by projected source-bound cues and not a claim to isolate hidden neural regions attention heads logits K/V cache or compute kernels
  + selected stitches bias the available continuation toward relevant distinctions and operations but do not force a result or prove semantic correctness
  + the host projects the selected set into every covered model call and releases or recompiles it when scope receipt observation authority or model profile changes

& [LearningAndCalibration]
  + optimality is relative to exact model version inference parameters task class horizon context assembly and success metric
  + begin with deterministic provider-free selection and synthetic controls before using live inference outcomes
  + later attributed calibration may compare term-set variants and retain which set reached accepted closure with fewer tokens calls reads corrections elapsed time and unsupported assumptions
  + historical outcomes are evidence for new candidates and weights rather than authority to bypass current requirements
  + exploration remains bounded so a previously successful stitch set cannot become an unexamined permanent prompt

& [ExperimentDirection]
  + compare no lookahead one stitch two stitches and a wider packet on equal tasks starting state model provider sampling tool policy and budgets
  + measure time to first correct operation time to accepted result input and output tokens tool calls redundant reads plan repairs gate failures unsupported assumptions and final requirement coverage
  + repeat across retrieval planning code change evidence closure and reentry task classes
  + speed improvement is accepted only when semantic quality authority correspondence safety and evidence completeness do not regress

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical selector scoring weights optimality claim satisfaction signature Rust host projection prompt mutation provider call live calibration workspace action autonomous execution remote work FPGA Minecraft or physical effect is authorized
